[Black "Black study side"]
[Result "*"]

{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O Be7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 7. e4 Nc6 8. Re1 Qc7 9. e5 Nd7 { Authored anchor. Advancing e5 gains space and displaces Nf6, but fixes a pawn that Black can undermine with ...f6. The f1 knight route is now a plan, not a forced continuation. } 10. Qe2 b5 { Plan: Improve Nf1-e3 or h2-g4 according to available squares, and use h4 only after inspecting ...f6. Keep d3 defended as Black expands. Opponent resource: Black can strike at the base or head of the chain. A dramatic wing attack fails if the center opens with your pieces misplaced. } *

