{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O Be7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 7. e4 dxe4 8. dxe4 { Authored anchor. The central exchange removes the familiar d5-e5 blockade. White's d-pawn becomes an e-pawn, opening the d-file and changing the bishop's prospects. } 8... b5 9. e5 Nd5 10. Re1 Bb7 { Plan: Develop on open files and compare piece activity. Use the e4 outpost control and consider Nc4 when it creates a real threat. Opponent resource: An automatic e5 attack plan may no longer fit. Black can use ...Nc6 and ...Qc7 to put pressure on e4. } *

