{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. O-O Be7 5. d3 c5 6. Nbd2 Nc6 7. e4 Qc7 { Authored anchor. Black has not declared the king's destination. White has no automatic target on g8 and should prepare useful central moves first. } 8. exd5 exd5 9. d4 b6 10. dxc5 bxc5 { Plan: Re1 supports e4; e5 can gain space if tactically justified. Wait to see whether Black castles or opens the center before committing the h-pawn. Opponent resource: A pawn storm toward an empty kingside wastes time. Black may answer by exchanging central pawns with the king still flexible. } *

