{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 e6 2. d3 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. Ngf3 c5 5. g3 Nc6 6. Bg2 Be7 7. O-O O-O 8. Re1 { Authored anchor. The same structural idea can be reached with 1.e4 and d3. Nd2 must precede Ngf3 here if White wants this exact arrangement without blocking a knight. } 8... Qc7 9. c3 h6 10. Qe2 Rd8 { Plan: Compare the position with the 1.Nf3 route by placing every piece, including the queen bishop. Learn the transposition once and keep both entry routes on the map. Opponent resource: Black is not forced to play ...Nf6 or ...Be7. Early ...dxe4 or a different bishop development changes the task. } *

