{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. O-O Bf5 5. d3 e6 6. c4 dxc4 7. dxc4 { Authored anchor. White changes the usual KIA pawn structure to challenge Black's center immediately. The d-pawn recapture opens the d-file and retains a central foothold. } 7... Qxd1 8. Rxd1 Bc2 9. Rd2 Bf5 10. Nh4 Nbd7 { Plan: Develop the queen knight and contest the open file. Decide whether a later e4 gains space or simply creates a target. Opponent resource: Black can exchange queens or use ...Nbd7 and ...Be7 to complete development. The position is now closer to a Reti structure than an e5 attack. } *

