{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. O-O Bf5 5. d3 e6 6. Nh4 Bg6 7. Nxg6 hxg6 { Authored anchor. White gives a knight for the active bishop and changes Black's kingside pawn structure. The open h-file can help Black as well as create targets. } 8. Nd2 Bd6 9. e4 Nbd7 10. d4 Nxe4 { Plan: Develop the remaining pieces and use the bishop pair in a position that may open. Do not assume doubled pawns alone justify a direct attack. Opponent resource: Black's h8 rook now has an open file. Castling short was already a commitment, so watch pressure toward your own king. } *

