{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c6 4. O-O Bg4 5. d3 Nbd7 6. Nbd2 e5 { Authored anchor. Black pins or pressures Nf3 and establishes a broad center. White needs a central plan before beginning a maneuvering attack. } 7. e4 dxe4 8. dxe4 h6 9. h3 Be6 10. Qe2 a5 { Plan: Consider e4 if it holds, or c4 to challenge d5. h3 can ask the bishop a question but should serve development rather than become an isolated tempo. Opponent resource: If Nf3 is exchanged, e4 may lose a defender. Count defenders after ...Bxf3 rather than before it. } *

