{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. e4 c6 2. d3 d5 3. Nd2 e5 4. Ngf3 Bd6 5. g3 Nf6 6. Bg2 O-O 7. O-O { Authored anchor. White can choose a KIA-style arrangement, but Black obtains an e5-d5 center and an active bishop. This is not the usual French target position. } 7... Bc7 8. c3 Re8 9. Qc2 a5 10. d4 Nxe4 { Plan: Challenge the center with c3 and possibly d4, or prepare exd5 when the resulting files favor your pieces. Maintain a safe e4 pawn. Opponent resource: Black may gain space with ...d4. A rehearsed e5 push is impossible while Black occupies e5. } *

