{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 c5 3. Bg2 Nc6 4. O-O e5 5. d3 Nf6 6. e4 d4 { Authored anchor. Black closes the center with a space advantage. White has a reversed King's Indian type of position, but the move order and extra tempo require independent calculation. } 7. a4 Bd6 8. Nfd2 a6 9. f4 h6 10. Qe2 Be6 { Plan: Prepare a kingside lever with appropriate knight moves or use c3 to question d4. Choose a side based on the fixed pawn chain and king locations. Opponent resource: Black can expand with ...b5 and ...c4. A slow maneuver must be measured against the opponent's actual pawn-break timing. } *

