{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 Nc6 2. g3 e5 3. d3 d5 4. Bg2 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 { Authored anchor. Black has gained a large center. White completes development while preparing a challenge; there is no obligation to finish every standard KIA move first. } 6. c4 O-O 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Nc3 Be6 9. d4 exd4 10. Nxd4 Nxd4 { Plan: Use c4 or e4 only after calculating exchanges. Develop the queen knight to a square that supports the chosen lever. Opponent resource: Black can push ...e4 to attack Nf3 if the pawn is supported. Watch that immediate threat before choosing a quiet move. } *

