{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 f5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 g6 4. O-O Bg7 5. d3 O-O 6. Nbd2 d6 7. e4 { Authored anchor. White challenges Black's kingside space through e4. Black's f-pawn move creates a different set of dark-square weaknesses and attacking chances. } 7... fxe4 8. Nxe4 Nxe4 9. dxe4 e5 10. a4 a5 { Plan: Calculate ...fxe4 and dxe4, develop the queen bishop and watch the e-file. A later c3 can prepare a central expansion. Opponent resource: Black may use ...e5 and ...Nc6 to support a broad center. The g7 bishop and f-file can become active after exchanges. } *

