{ Original King's Indian Attack course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. Nf3 d5 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 c5 4. d3 Nc6 5. Nbd2 e5 6. e4 dxe4 7. dxe4 { Authored anchor. White delays castling while constructing the center. The exchange on e4 opens the d-file and makes queen exchanges a practical possibility. } 7... Be7 8. c3 b5 9. Qe2 Rb8 10. O-O O-O { Plan: Compare castling with a useful queen move, then develop the queen bishop. Open-file control may matter more than preserving queens for an attack. Opponent resource: Black can exchange queens if the file opens completely. Evaluate the king's destination in the resulting endgame rather than fearing a lost castling right automatically. } *

